  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with an approved budget of $2 million, which was later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses to cover real-time analytics integration. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase, the testing phase, and the achievement of the first major milestone ahead of schedule with a tested secure file sharing prototype. The team is currently in the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, and has expanded by adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Upcoming events include an onboarding session for new members on September 10th, a celebration for the testing milestone on October 10th, and planned user interface enhancements in October. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
}
